    {
      "id": "claim_49b64a26a99846a995d9aff3fee06dab",
      "statement": "A green hermetic pytest run proves no container behaviour: the ubuntu-latest runner has no podman so every HARNESSED_PODMAN-gated integration test skips there by design, the suite runs no `podman build` and no `harnessed container-run`, and the run prints a \"live verification\" section naming what did not execute — a skip is not a pass, and before live.yml existed those tests ran nowhere with only the skip count as a trace.",
